  "body": "Hello - \n\nI stumbled across the repository since I was working on the same general area (nvidia-compatible musl).  I started reviewing your patches with what I've understood so far and I have a questions about your initial-exec TLS implementation.\n\nI believe that your implementation allocates a static area that needs to be at least as large as every shared library (with tls) before it loads the initial-exec tls shared libraries:\n\n1. lib1.so (tls dynamic)\n2. lib2.so (tls dynamic)\n3. lib3.so (tls dynamic)\n4. lib4.so (tls initial-exec)\n5. lib5.so (tls dynamic)\n\nThe static area must be at least lib{1,2,3,4} TLS-sized int the current implementation for lib4.so to work.\n\n_Okay this is the area I'm less sure of now_, but maybe you have a better understanding:\n\n- Also, lib1,2,3 will be using the new area installed by `install_new_tls`\n- So we are wasting a few hundred bytes in the static area?\n\nI've been thinking about a more complete solution where the static area is tracked separately and only used on dlopening initial-exec tls libraries.  It might be overengineered because it seems like shared libraries don't often use a lot of TLS, but still - could be nice to have a full solution!\n\nP.S. If you get a notification about a comment (on a commit) that is no longer there - it's because I realised that I was wrong!",
